  "body": "## What changed\n\n**#637 step E1** (fork synced at v0.16.0; branched from upstream/main). The design for step E - the holders' mutation path, the two routes for cutting a carried field, the build order - is on the issue (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/637#issuecomment-6787218007); E2a-c are filed as #779, #780, #781 and the holders stay #586's. This PR is the first slice, which stands alone: **a field column's floor under a cut is read exactly**, so `CarriedField::column_body` (step D) carries through-holes, through-slots and floor slivers instead of refusing the whole carry.\n\n- **The monotone law** (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/field_floor.rs`): every tool `Stock::simulate` builds spans the verdict world above its tip (`spanning_flank`), so its swept solid holds every point above any point it holds. A column's material is therefore one interval `[shell floor, tool bottom]` or nothing: a cut from above lowers the top and never raises the floor. New `SdfField::column_span(x, y) -> ColumnSpan { Material { top, floor } | Empty | CutFromBelow | Unreadable }`:\n  - the down-march's `Top` proves a material centre, so the floor is the shell's lowest crossing (exact);\n  - `NoMaterial` is cut through OR a sliver thinner than a cell with no centre in it; the cut layer's own ray-entry record (`cut_ups`) at the cell below the floor plane gives the tool's bottom (`centre + entry`, closed-form under a flat floor), and material stands iff it is not below the floor - the column body's `top < floor` empty law, same strictness;\n  - a record that must exist and does not is refused by name (`Unreadable`), never read as air.\n- **A bounded tool suspends the law.** A solid that does not span the world above its tip - the truncated taper (`backend.rs`'s \"chimney\"), a bare ball, a lathe sweep, a posed axis - sets `bounded_cuts` on the field (`subtract_batch`, past every gate so a refusal leaves the field as it stood; `Sweep::spans_above`, `ArcPiece::spans_above`), and a floor a cut came within a cell of is then refused as step B refused every cut (`CutFromBelow`).\n- `floor_at` keeps its API as `column_span`'s floor; `field_body::read_column` reads one `column_span` per column (one march instead of one march plus a floor read).\n- **A column reads at its cell centre.** A query a hair inside a cut whose cell centre stands outside reads as its cell does (the field's `distance` / `column_top` law): material over-reported at the lattice's resolution, never air where steel stands. The #649-review test now pins that contract instead of the refusal.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/637-carried-stock-field.md` (route (ii) over (i), the dropped `cut_downs`-at-every-claim, the dropped lattice origin).\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (sim: 27 suites incl. `stock_backend_parity`, `stock_field_cost`, `carry_engine_agreement`; motion `posed_subtract`; app `stock_export`, `verify`): green on the final head (2.2 min; sim 27 suites, motion, app all ok)\n- Pinning tests:\n  - `field_floor`: `a_slot_through_the_plate_reads_empty_and_its_neighbours_exact`, `a_sliver_on_the_floor_is_read_from_the_record` (0.2 under a 0.5 cell, exact to 1e-12; the zero-height tie; a hair below is cut through), `a_bounded_tool_keeps_the_refusal_by_name`, `a_column_reads_at_its_cell_centre_near_a_cut_wall`, `an_uncut_floor_reads_the_shell_exactly`.\n  - `field_body`: `a_slot_through_the_plate_carries_its_columns_empty` (volume 960 = 1440 - the slot), `a_floor_a_bounded_tool_reached_refuses_the_carry_by_name`.\n  - `carry_engine_agreement`: two new fixtures - `a_slot_through_the_block_carries_the_same_on_both_engines` and `a_sliver_on_the_floor_carries_the_same_on_both_engines` - both engines agree per column on `empty_at`, top and floor to 1e-6 through all 8 turns.\n- Clippy `-p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Linux batch gate: green on the final head 7c1bc3ba (14.3 min, 9 steps, 0 failed: geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion incl. slow, app incl. slow, ui, clippy)\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Nothing shipped changes: the column engine is still the default, the field's down-march is untouched, and `stock_backend_parity` / `stock_engine_agreement` / the app carry suites (`setup_carry`, `carried_verify`, `rest_across_setups`) are unchanged - no golden or snapshot touched.\n- Cuts AFTER a carry on the field (E2a-c, #779-#781) and the app holders (#586): nothing in the app calls `column_span` yet.\n- A sliver under a ball or bull floor is read from the searched entry (conservative to below, the `field_ray` direction) - exact to the search floor, not closed-form; the agreement fixtures use the flat floor.\n\nChangelog: none (internal: the field column's floor under a cut reads exactly; not yet used by the app)\n\nEffort: max (design + E1; not escalated)\n\nRefs #637\nRefs #26\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
